      "kind": "why_it_matters",
      "title": "Shiloh and the Festival",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_3",
          "text": "Shiloh is presented as a named regional gathering place, with a yearly festival and a detailed route description. Archaeological remains show occupation at Shiloh, but they cannot by themselves identify the festival, the tent of meeting, Micah\u2019s shrine, or the Danite installation. This distinction keeps the passage\u2019s setting clear without treating material remains as proof of every narrated event or structure.",
